    "summary": "Meta Platforms, parent of Facebook and Instagram, is set to face a landmark trial in California brought by 29 US states alleging deliberate design to addict young users. The trial begins August 18, with a verdict expected in October.",
    "content": "Meta Platforms, the parent company of Facebook and Instagram, will stand trial this week in a case filed by 29 US states accusing the firm of deliberately designing its social media platforms to be addictive among minors. The case, which could result in $1.4 billion in penalties, is being heard in federal court in Oakland, California, starting Monday, August 18, and is expected to run for seven weeks.\n\nThe lawsuit alleges that Meta knowingly used psychological features on its apps to keep young users engaged for extended periods, despite internal research indicating potential harm. The states argue these tactics violate consumer protection laws and have contributed to a mental health crisis among adolescents.\n\nDistrict Judge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers will preside over the proceedings, with a final ruling anticipated in October. This trial is notable as it is one of the largest legal challenges concerning youth and social media in the US, setting a potential precedent for how tech companies oversee platform safety.\n\nThe outcomes could have implications for the Somali diaspora, who often use Facebook and Instagram to maintain cultural ties, share news, and communicate with relatives. If the lawsuit results in stricter regulations, these platforms may change their algorithms or add safeguards, affecting how diaspora communities interact online.\n\nLegal experts suggest that the case may push social media companies to prioritize user well-being ahead of engagement metrics, which could reshape the digital environment for all users. For Somali parents in the diaspora, this trial draws attention to the need for digital literacy and monitoring of online activities among young people.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Dalsan here: https://radiodalsan.com/2026/08/15/meta-oo-wajahaysa-dacwad-1-4-tirilyan-ah/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=meta-oo-wajahaysa-dacwad-1-4-tirilyan-ah",
